<item>
            <title>[LU-20453] mdc: fix memory leak in mdc_device_alloc() when class_name2obd() fails</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20453</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;In `mdc_device_alloc()`, when `class_name2obd()` fails to find the OBD device, the function returns an error without freeing the `osc_device` structure that was allocated earlier. This causes a memory leak on the client side during failed device initialization attempts.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
